Codex Usage Monitor
Copyright (c) 2026 Théophile Diot

This is an independent GNOME application with an original interface.

History sampling, notification state transitions, and asynchronous GNOME I/O
foundations are adapted from Claude Usage Tracker for Linux by Théophile Diot:
https://github.com/TheophileDiot/Claude-Usage-Tracker-Linux

That project's foundations include Claude Usage Tracker by its contributors
(https://github.com/hamed-elfayome/Claude-Usage-Tracker) and Claude Code Usage
by Baptiste-Pasquier (https://github.com/Haletran/claude-usage-extension).
Their applicable MIT copyright notices and permission terms remain in LICENSE.
This project does not reuse their branding, icon, or Claude statusline renderer.

Codex protocol and native footer identifiers are documented by OpenAI:
https://github.com/openai/codex
Codex itself is not bundled or modified. It is installed separately by the user.

The panel's OpenAI Blossom icon identifies the monitored OpenAI service. It is
an unmodified asset from https://cdn.openai.com/brand/OpenAI-Logos-2025.zip.
The OpenAI and ChatGPT marks belong to OpenAI and are subject to its brand usage
terms (https://openai.com/brand/), not this project's MIT license.

This project is unofficial and is not affiliated with or endorsed by OpenAI.
